Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted).
Source: https://github.com/qt/qtbase/blob/v6.12.0/src/gui/kernel/qguiapplication.cpp

Ignore constructor-time theme notifications until the platform theme is installed.
A synchronous QPA can deliver QKdeTheme::refresh() before createPlatformTheme()
returns. Initial style hints, palette, fonts and theme hints are read after
installation. Keep all theme-change delivery after installation unchanged.

--- src/gui/kernel/qguiapplication.cpp.orig
+++ src/gui/kernel/qguiapplication.cpp
@@ -2825,7 +2825,9 @@ void QGuiApplicationPrivate::processThemeChanged(QWindowSystemInterfacePrivate::ThemeChangeEvent *)
     // FIXME: Remove check once we ensure that the platform plugin is
     // torn down before QGuiApplication.
-    if (!qGuiApp)
+    // A theme can notify us from its constructor before it is installed.
+    // Initial theme state is read after platform integration initialization.
+    if (!qGuiApp || !platformTheme())
         return;
 
     if (auto *guiAppPrivate = QGuiApplicationPrivate::instance())
         guiAppPrivate->handleThemeChanged();
